      {
        "id": 199588,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-09T17:00:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MarioFanaticXV\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/48/2129_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MarioFanaticXV:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, because setup takes so much longer, I almost never play them with the physical version- shuffling 5 to 7 decks is enough as it is, shuffling 8 to 12 is a lot of extra work I don't want to go through just to play. That being said, I am much more willing to play them in the digital version.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's the reason that I never play a 'solitare' style with Vengeance. Every player is responsible for a hero and a villain, suffling and up-keep and all. Makes thing slightly easier if you divide up the bookkeeping. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>But if I want to play by myself, then the videogame is perfect.</p>",
